1. A method of positioning a workpiece in a metal sawing machine, the method comprising:

entering, into a control system of the metal sawing machine, an offset value relative to a zero reference position for calibrating a front end of the workpiece;

actuating clamping jaws to engage the workpiece and move the front end of the workpiece to a cutting plane of the metal sawing machine based at least in part on the offset value;

returning the clamping jaws to an initial position after the front end of the workpiece has been brought to the cutting plane;

reclamping the workpiece with the clamping jaws; and

feeding the workpiece from the initial position to a desired cutting position for performing a cutting operation.

1. A method for positioning a workpiece in a sawing machine having a cutting plane, a zero position associated with the cutting plane, and clamping jaws configured to clamp and feed the workpiece, the method comprising:

   positioning the clamping jaws at an initial position;

   determining an offset corresponding to a distance between a front end of the workpiece and the zero position in the cutting plane;

   moving the clamping jaws by the offset while the workpiece is clamped, thereby repositioning the workpiece relative to the cutting plane;

   releasing the clamping jaws from the workpiece after the repositioning;

   resetting the clamping jaws to the initial position;

   reclamping the workpiece with the clamping jaws; and

   feeding the workpiece with the clamping jaws from the initial position to a sawing position for performing a sawing operation.
